cff-version: 1.2.0
title: The Measurement Axioms
message: >-
  If you reference this doctrine or the specification extracted from it, please
  cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ali Toygar
    family-names: Abak
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3718-4010
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-02'
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A governance verdict is a measurement of a claim about a system, and a
  measurement that was not taken must not be reported as one that passed. The
  doctrine states seven axioms and five properties of a governance measurement
  path, defines a six-value verdict algebra with two collapse prohibitions, and
  is accompanied by a normative specification, a machine-readable record schema,
  conformance requirements and a reference implementation.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - assurance
  - conformance
  - evidence
  - measurement validity
references:
  - type: report
    title: >-
      Phionyx self-audit against The Measurement Axioms
    authors:
      - given-names: Ali Toygar
        family-names: Abak
    date-released: '2026-08-01'
    notes: >-
      The doctrine applied to its own authors' runtime. Twelve findings, none
      with verification_status pass at the time of release.
